      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T20:35:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could increase the timeout, but in the bug, there appeared to be a 4 second delay before the thread ran, so the timeout would need to be more than that, and so the question would be: how long do you need to make it?\n\nHowever, I don\u0027t understand what is special about this path that means a timeout is warranted. Why is this more likely to stall forever as compared with any other part of the Bluetooth stack? I don\u0027t see anything special about the code path this follows: it\u0027s just a small amount of initiasation as far as I can tell (but the code is new to me so I might be missing something).\n\nIf nothing distinguishes this code path from other similar code paths that don\u0027t have a timeout, then I don\u0027t believe a timeout is warranted here. With or without a timer here, a bug would still need to be fixed if there were an issue here.",
