      "side": 1,
      "message": "4 seconds... what takes so long !?! \n\nFYI the overall timeout to start the Bluetooth is expected to take 4 seconds ([link](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/btservice/AdapterState.java;l\u003d255;drc\u003de53a42a1dd57ec252ffe1ed14113f5329ffe44f9) / a bit more on slow devices). So if just the rust init take that much time, there is probably something off.\n\nBut you are making a good point. A failure here could just block the whole stack and be investigated as any other lock contention in the stack, without the need to make another timeout.",
